# Compiled Hale binaries — produced by `hale build` next to source.
#
# Hale places the binary in the same directory as its main.hl, named
# after the directory (examples/<demo>/<demo>), plus sometimes a
# `main` binary from intermediate builds. CI / consumers should
# rebuild from .hl source.
#
# Generic rule: ignore everything under examples/, then un-ignore
# directories (so git can descend) and any file with an extension.
# Demo binaries are extensionless, so they stay ignored. NOTE: an
# extensionless *source* file (Procfile, Makefile) added under an
# examples/ dir must be force-added (`git add -f`) or given an
# explicit `!` rule here.
**/examples/**
!**/examples/**/
!**/examples/**/*.*

# Library-root binaries (a CLI shape, e.g. migrations/migrations)
/migrations/migrations

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
